#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""cycle: one build-and-test cycle of phases 6 and 7 in one command: merge, compile, format and lint, test, look,
cut each fixer's packet, send it to the same fixer, record the cycle.

usage: cycle LABEL [--fixers FILE] [--tracks SRC] [--groups DIR] [--batch B] [--area A]...
             [--no-merge] [--no-lint] [--no-tests] [--no-look] [--no-send] [--dry-run] [--config PORT.TOML]

  LABEL          the cycle's run label (`<batch>-run-<n>`): the app run is LABEL, the framework trials LABEL-fw, the
                 compile LABEL-compile, all under work.runs.
  --fixers FILE  the round's fixers, one per line `TASK [fw:BRANCH] [app:BRANCH]` (# comments and blank lines
                 skipped). TASK is the fixer's board task and swarm.py task; for a red fixer it is also its track id
                 in the tracks file. A line with no branch means `red/<TASK>` in each integration tree that has it.
  --tracks SRC   which tests each red fixer owns (groups.md, a split-failures.py directory or a TSV), for
                 compare-runs.py and diag-cut.py.
  --groups DIR   split-errors.py output: a compile or lint error that no fixer's branch touched goes to the group
                 that owns its file (`<stem>.files`, else the files `<stem>.errors` names), task `cfix-<stem>`.
                 --fixers, --tracks and --groups default to the values of the previous cycle (its cycle.json).
  --batch B, --area A   the batch and areas the cycle serves. When they differ from the board's, cycle records
                 them (`track phase <current phase> --batch B --area A`). The areas pick the look panels.
  --no-merge, --no-lint, --no-tests, --no-look, --no-send   leave that step out.
  --dry-run      print the steps and their commands with the resolved fixers, branches, crates and fixer mode; run
                 nothing.

Steps:
  1. merge   Refuses (exit 2) when an integration tree has uncommitted changes. `git merge --no-ff --no-edit` of
             each fixer branch into framework.integration (fw:) or app.integration (app:). On a conflict it aborts
             that merge, merges nothing more and stops (exit 3), naming the branch and the files. A branch whose
             merge an earlier cycle's guard reverted (cycle.json `reverted`) is skipped while it has no new commits;
             with new commits, the cycle first reverts that revert, so the earlier commits come back with the new.
  2. compile `compile-gate LABEL-compile`. Its exit 2 stops the cycle.
  3. lint    Only after a clean compile, on the crates that own files changed since framework.writing_base and
             app.writing_base (crates under a `vendor/` directory left out): `cl cargo fmt -p <crate>...`, committed
             as one `cycle LABEL: cargo fmt` commit per tree when it changed anything; then clippy with warnings
             denied and the doc build with RUSTDOCFLAGS="-D warnings", through `cl cargo` on cl's own selection
             (framework: the crates plus feature-root with the `cl features` of each crate; app: every package of
             `[workspace.metadata.cl] selection`), so no second feature set builds. A finding in a crate that did not
             change is listed and not counted.
  4. tests   Only after a clean compile: the framework trials, `test-run LABEL --app`, then
             `compare-runs.py LABEL --tracks SRC --out <run>/tracks.md --json <run>/attribution.json` with a
             `--branch TASK=TREE:PRE..MERGE` per new merge, and `diag-cut.py LABEL --tracks SRC`.
             Merge guard, in a red round: a fixer that compare-runs marks `likely` for more newly failing tests
             (passing in the previous run) than its track fixed gets each of its merges of this cycle reverted
             (`git revert -m 1`, one commit per tree), recorded in cycle.json `reverted` with the revert sha, before
             the cycle records. Its packet lists those tests. A revert that conflicts is aborted and noted.
             Framework trials: in a red round (tracks and fixers given), `test-run LABEL-fw --fw C ...` over each
             red fixer's own crates (the packages owning the framework files its merged commits changed, in this
             and earlier cycles) plus the crates whose trials failed in the previous cycle; when those and the app
             run are green, `test-run LABEL-fw-rest` runs every other crate changed since plan.base before the cycle
             reports green. Otherwise (a compile cycle, a batch's first run) `test-run LABEL-fw --fw`.
  5. look    When the app half compiled and look.driver is set: `cl <look.port_build>` in app.integration, then
             `look pair` for each states file with a state of one of the cycle's areas (all of them when no area
             is known). Skipped, and said so, while look.port_build is unset.
  6. packets One file per fixer in <work.runs>/LABEL/followup/<TASK>.md: a header with the cycle, the fixer mode
             (pipeline.fixer_mode, `auto` decided by build.warm_check_s, build.full_run_s and build.fw_trial_s) and
             the call budget (pipeline.fixer_calls); in build mode with a build pool, the fixer's build trees
             (`build-pool take TASK`; with no slot free that fixer works code-only this round); the fixer's diag-cut
             packet; and the compile errors and lint findings in files its group owns (--groups) or its merged
             commits changed. A fixer with no failing test, no finding and no `DIAG ` line left on its branches gets
             no packet; its task goes to done and gives its build slot back.
  7. send    `swarm.py --follow-up TASK <packet>` for each packet, pipeline.parallel at a time, and waits for every
             fixer to hand back, at most pipeline.followup_timeout_min minutes each; a fixer past it is stalled.
             Nothing is sent while the board is paused.
  8. record  <work.runs>/LABEL/report.md and cycle.json, one row in <work.runs>/cycles.tsv, one `cycle` event, the
             lead session's cost (`track usage`'s sample, when it runs from the lead's shell), and
             in phase 6 after a clean compile `track phase 7` (the phase gate decides; a refusal is listed).
  9. upstream  Fetches framework.branch and app.base_branch into refs/portkit/upstream/ of the integration trees
             (portkit/sync.py) and notes "sync due" when a tree is more than land.sync_after_commits behind, or
             behind with its last tools/sync more than a day ago. On a green cycle, when land.early_ci_fork is set and
             the framework head is not the newest ref in <work.landing>/early-ci.tsv, it notes the
             `land/early-ci.sh` command; it never runs it. A failed fetch is a note. Also in --dry-run.

Result: cycle.json, and the last stdout line
  cycle LABEL: exit N; merged k/n; compile: ...; lint: ...; app: ...; reverted: ...; look: ...; packets: ...; mode M; T s
cycle.json `red` (a red round): the fixer mode, the fixers' models, the pass delta against the previous cycle and the
follow-ups' cost, also in report.md and the cycle event (process/costs.md, "Red rounds by fixer model").
cycles.tsv columns: label, start (UTC), phase, batch, area, mode, merge_s, compile_s, lint_s, test_s, look_s,
send_s, total_s, gap_s (start minus the previous cycle's end), errors (compile errors plus counted lint findings),
failing (app tests failing outside work.baseline_failures), exit.

Exit status: 0 green (compiles, lint clean, no failing test outside the baseline, no stalled fixer, no merge
reverted), 1 work left,
2 a tool failure or a dirty integration tree, 3 a merge conflict.
"""
from __future__ import annotations

import argparse
import json
import os
import re
import shlex
import subprocess
import sys
import time
import tomllib
from concurrent.futures import ThreadPoolExecutor
from datetime import datetime, timezone
from pathlib import Path

sys.path.insert(0, str(Path(__file__).resolve().parent))
from portkit import config, gates, track  # noqa: E402
from portkit import sync as upstream_sync  # noqa: E402
from portkit.pool import Pool, PoolError, SetupError  # noqa: E402
from portkit import track as T  # noqa: E402
from portkit.testlog import load_tracks  # noqa: E402

TOOLS = Path(__file__).resolve().parent
REPOS = {"fw": "framework.integration", "app": "app.integration"}
BASES = {"fw": "framework.writing_base", "app": "app.writing_base"}
TSV_COLS = ("label", "start", "phase", "batch", "area", "mode", "merge_s", "compile_s", "lint_s", "test_s", "look_s",
            "send_s", "total_s", "gap_s", "errors", "failing", "exit")
EXIT_GREEN, EXIT_LEFT, EXIT_TOOL, EXIT_CONFLICT = 0, 1, 2, 3


class Stop(Exception):
    def __init__(self, code: int, why: str):
        super().__init__(why)
        self.code, self.why = code, why


def git(tree: Path, *args: str, check: bool = True) -> subprocess.CompletedProcess:
    r = subprocess.run(["git", "-C", str(tree), *args], capture_output=True, text=True)
    if check and r.returncode != 0:
        raise Stop(EXIT_TOOL, f"git {' '.join(args)} in {tree}: {r.stderr.strip()[:300]}")
    return r


def utc(t: float) -> str:
    return datetime.fromtimestamp(t, timezone.utc).strftime("%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ")


class Cycle:
    def __init__(self, cfg, a):
        self.cfg, self.a = cfg, a
        self.runs = cfg.path("work.runs")
        self.rd = gates.run_dir(cfg, a.label)
        self.env = gates.cl_env(cfg)
        self.trees = {r: cfg.path(k) for r, k in REPOS.items() if cfg.get(k)}
        self.mode = cfg.fixer_mode()
        self.t0 = time.time()
        self.secs: dict[str, float] = {}
        self.prev = self.previous()
        self.out: dict = {"label": a.label, "start": utc(self.t0), "mode": self.mode, "notes": []}
        # {task: {repo: {"revert", "branch", "tip", "merge"}}}: merges the guard reverted and that stay reverted.
        self.reverted: dict[str, dict[str, dict]] = {
            t: dict(rs) for t, rs in ((self.prev or {}).get("reverted") or {}).items()}
        self.regressions: dict[str, list[dict]] = {}

    # ------------------------------------------------------------ inputs
    def previous(self) -> dict | None:
        f = self.runs / "cycles.tsv"
        if not f.is_file():
            return None
        rows = [l.split("\t") for l in f.read_text().splitlines()[1:] if l.strip()]
        rows = [r for r in rows if r and r[0] != self.a.label]
        if not rows:
            return None
        try:
            return json.loads((self.runs / rows[-1][0] / "cycle.json").read_text())
        except (OSError, ValueError):
            return None

    def inherit(self, name: str) -> str | None:
        v = getattr(self.a, name)
        if v:
            return str(Path(v).resolve())
        return (self.prev or {}).get("inputs", {}).get(name)

    def fixers(self) -> list[dict]:
        f = self.inherit("fixers")
        if not f:
            return []
        out = []
        for n, line in enumerate(Path(f).read_text().splitlines(), 1):
            line = line.split("#", 1)[0].strip()
            if not line:
                continue
            task, *specs = line.split()
            T.check_task(task)
            branches = {}
            for sp in specs:
                repo, sep, br = sp.partition(":")
                if not sep or repo not in REPOS or not br:
                    raise Stop(EXIT_TOOL, f"{f}:{n}: branch {sp!r}: write fw:BRANCH or app:BRANCH")
                branches[repo] = br
            if not specs:
                for repo, tree in self.trees.items():
                    if git(tree, "rev-parse", "--verify", "-q", f"refs/heads/red/{task}", check=False).returncode == 0:
                        branches[repo] = f"red/{task}"
            out.append({"task": task, "branches": branches})
        return out

    def board(self):
        try:
            s = T.open_store(self.a.config)
            return s.state() if s else None
        except Exception as e:   # the cycle's work does not depend on the board
            self.out["notes"].append(f"board not read: {e}")
            return None

    # ------------------------------------------------------------ helpers
    def timed(self, step: str, fn, *args):
        t = time.time()
        try:
            return fn(*args)
        finally:
            self.secs[step] = self.secs.get(step, 0) + time.time() - t

    def tool(self, name: str, *args: str, log: str) -> int:
        cmd = ([sys.executable, "-I", str(TOOLS / name)] if name.endswith(".py") else [str(TOOLS / name)]) + list(args)
        with open(self.rd / log, "wb") as f:
            rc = subprocess.run(cmd, stdout=f, stderr=subprocess.STDOUT).returncode
        last = (self.rd / log).read_text(errors="replace").strip().splitlines()
        print(f"{name}: exit {rc}" + (f": {last[-1][:300]}" if last else ""), flush=True)
        return rc

    def changed_crates(self, repo: str) -> list[str]:
        tree, base = self.trees.get(repo), self.cfg.get(BASES[repo])
        if not tree or not base:
            return []
        crates = set()
        for f in gates.changed_files(tree, base):
            if "/vendor/" in "/" + f:
                continue
            p = gates.package_of(tree, f)
            if p:
                crates.add(p)
        return sorted(crates)

    def selection(self) -> list[str]:
        m = self.trees["app"] / "Cargo.toml"
        try:
            return list(tomllib.loads(m.read_text())["workspace"]["metadata"]["cl"]["selection"])
        except (OSError, KeyError, tomllib.TOMLDecodeError) as e:
            raise Stop(EXIT_TOOL, f"{m}: no [workspace.metadata.cl] selection ({e})")

    # ------------------------------------------------------------ 1. merge
    def merge(self, fixers: list[dict]) -> list[dict]:
        for repo, tree in self.trees.items():
            if git(tree, "status", "--porcelain", "-uno").stdout.strip():
                raise Stop(EXIT_TOOL, f"{REPOS[repo]} ({tree}) has uncommitted changes; commit or remove them first")
        done = []
        earlier = {t: dict(rs) for t, rs in self.reverted.items()}
        for fx in fixers:
            for repo, br in fx["branches"].items():
                tree = self.trees[repo]
                pre = git(tree, "rev-parse", "HEAD").stdout.strip()
                restore = None
                rv = (earlier.get(fx["task"]) or {}).get(repo)
                if rv and rv.get("branch") == br:
                    tip = git(tree, "rev-parse", br).stdout.strip()
                    if tip == rv.get("tip"):   # nothing new since the revert: it stays reverted
                        done.append({"task": fx["task"], "repo": repo, "branch": br, "sha": pre, "pre": pre,
                                     "files": [], "new": False, "skipped": "reverted, no new commits"})
                        continue
                    # The reverted commits are reachable already: a plain merge would bring only the new ones.
                    r = git(tree, "revert", "--no-edit", rv["revert"], check=False)
                    if r.returncode != 0:
                        git(tree, "revert", "--abort", check=False)
                        done.append({"task": fx["task"], "repo": repo, "branch": br, "conflict": ["(restoring "
                                     f"the reverted merge {rv['revert'][:10]})"]})
                        self.out["merged"] = done
                        raise Stop(EXIT_CONFLICT, f"restoring the reverted merge of {br} in {REPOS[repo]} "
                                                  f"(git revert {rv['revert'][:10]}) conflicts; resolve it on the "
                                                  "integration branch, then run the cycle again")
                    restore = git(tree, "rev-parse", "HEAD").stdout.strip()
                    self.reverted[fx["task"]].pop(repo)
                    if not self.reverted[fx["task"]]:
                        del self.reverted[fx["task"]]
                files = git(tree, "diff", "--name-only", f"{restore or pre}...{br}").stdout.split()
                r = git(tree, "merge", "--no-ff", "--no-edit", "-m", f"cycle {self.a.label}: merge {br}", br, check=False)
                if r.returncode != 0:
                    conflicted = git(tree, "diff", "--name-only", "--diff-filter=U", check=False).stdout.split()
                    git(tree, "merge", "--abort", check=False)
                    done.append({"task": fx["task"], "repo": repo, "branch": br, "conflict": conflicted or ["?"]})
                    self.out["merged"] = done
                    raise Stop(EXIT_CONFLICT, f"merge of {br} into {REPOS[repo]} conflicts in "
                                              f"{', '.join(conflicted) or r.stderr.strip()[:200]}; resolve it on the "
                                              f"integration branch, then run the cycle again")
                head = git(tree, "rev-parse", "HEAD").stdout.strip()
                done.append({"task": fx["task"], "repo": repo, "branch": br, "sha": head, "pre": pre, "files": files,
                             "new": head != pre, **({"restore": restore} if restore else {})})
            track.event("merge", f"cycle {self.a.label}: merged {', '.join(fx['branches'].values()) or 'nothing'}",
                        task=fx["task"])
        return done

    def touched(self, merged: list[dict]) -> dict[str, dict[str, set]]:
        """{task: {repo: files its merged commits changed}}, this cycle's plus the earlier cycles'."""
        out: dict[str, dict[str, set]] = {}
        for task, repos in ((self.prev or {}).get("touched") or {}).items():
            for repo, files in repos.items():
                out.setdefault(task, {}).setdefault(repo, set()).update(files)
        for m in merged:
            out.setdefault(m["task"], {}).setdefault(m["repo"], set()).update(m.get("files") or [])
        return out

    # ------------------------------------------------------------ 2. compile
    def compile(self) -> dict:
        rc = self.tool("compile-gate", f"{self.a.label}-compile", log="compile.log")
        try:
            s = json.loads((self.runs / f"{self.a.label}-compile" / "summary.json").read_text())
        except (OSError, ValueError):
            raise Stop(EXIT_TOOL, f"compile-gate exit {rc} and no summary.json")
        if rc == 2:
            raise Stop(EXIT_TOOL, f"compile-gate: tool failure (exit 2); see {self.rd / 'compile.log'}")
        fw, app = s.get("framework") or {}, s.get("app") or {}
        d = self.runs / f"{self.a.label}-compile"
        errs = {"fw": _lines(d / "fw.errors"), "app": _lines(d / "app.errors")}
        return {"exit": rc, "fw_errors": fw.get("errors", 0), "app_status": app.get("status"),
                "app_errors": app.get("errors", 0), "errors": errs, "unlinked": self.unlinked()}

    def unlinked(self) -> list[str]:
        """New .rs files (since each repo's writing base) that no `mod` line reaches: they are never built. Printed, not a
        failure."""
        found = []
        for repo, tree in self.trees.items():
            base = self.cfg.get(BASES[repo])
            if not base:
                continue
            new = subprocess.run(["git", "-C", str(tree), "diff", "--name-only", "--diff-filter=A", base, "HEAD", "--", "*.rs"],
                                 capture_output=True, text=True).stdout.split()
            if not new:
                continue
            tracked = subprocess.run(["git", "-C", str(tree), "ls-files", "*.rs"], capture_output=True, text=True).stdout
            out = subprocess.run([sys.executable, "-I", str(TOOLS / "mod-lines.py"), "--unlinked", *new], input=tracked,
                                 cwd=tree, capture_output=True, text=True).stdout
            found += [f"{repo}: {line}" for line in out.splitlines()]
        for line in found:
            print(f"UNLINKED {line}", flush=True)
        (self.rd / "unlinked.txt").write_text("".join(f"{x}\n" for x in found))
        return found

    # ------------------------------------------------------------ 3. lint
    def lint(self) -> dict:
        res = {"fmt": {}, "findings": {}, "outside": {}, "commands": []}
        for repo in self.trees:
            crates = self.changed_crates(repo)
            if not crates:
                continue
            tree = self.trees[repo]
            self.run_cl(tree, ["cargo", "fmt", *[x for c in crates for x in ("-p", c)]], f"lint-{repo}-fmt.log", res)
            if git(tree, "status", "--porcelain", "-uno").stdout.strip():
                git(tree, "commit", "-q", "-a", "-m", f"cycle {self.a.label}: cargo fmt")
                res["fmt"][repo] = git(tree, "rev-parse", "HEAD").stdout.strip()
            if repo == "fw":
                feats = []
                for c in crates:
                    r = subprocess.run(gates.cl(self.cfg, ["features", c]), cwd=tree, env=self.env, capture_output=True,
                                       text=True)
                    feats += [f for f in r.stdout.strip().split(",") if f]
                pk = [x for c in crates + ["feature-root"] for x in ("-p", c)] + (["--features", ",".join(feats)] if feats else [])
                clippy = ["cargo", "clippy", *pk, "--tests"]
                doc = ["cargo", "doc", "--no-deps", *pk]
            else:
                pk = [x for c in self.selection() for x in ("-p", c)]
                clippy = ["cargo", "clippy", "--lib", "--tests", *pk]
                doc = ["cargo", "doc", "--no-deps", *pk]
            common = ["--keep-going", "--message-format", "short"]
            found = []
            for kind, args, extra in (("clippy", clippy + common + ["--", "-D", "warnings"], {}),
                                      ("doc", doc + common, {"RUSTDOCFLAGS": "-D warnings"})):
                log = self.rd / f"lint-{repo}-{kind}.log"
                rc = self.run_cl(tree, args, log.name, res, extra)
                lines = gates.error_lines(log)
                if rc != 0 and not lines:
                    raise Stop(EXIT_TOOL, f"{kind} in {REPOS[repo]}: exit {rc} with no error line; see {log}")
                found += [f"{kind}: {l}" for l in lines]
            mine = [f for f in found if gates.package_of(tree, f.split(": ", 1)[1].split(":", 1)[0]) in crates]
            res["findings"][repo] = mine
            res["outside"][repo] = [f for f in found if f not in mine]
        res["count"] = sum(len(v) for v in res["findings"].values())
        return res

    def run_cl(self, tree: Path, args: list[str], log: str, res: dict, extra: dict | None = None) -> int:
        res["commands"].append("cl " + " ".join(shlex.quote(x) for x in args))
        f = self.rd / log
        f.write_bytes(b"")
        return gates.run_logged(gates.cl(self.cfg, args), tree, f, {**self.env, **(extra or {})})

    # ------------------------------------------------------------ 4. tests
    def fw_crates(self, fixers: list[dict], touched: dict) -> dict[str, list[str]] | None:
        """{task: its own framework crates} for a red round: the packages owning the framework files each fixer's
        merged commits changed. None when the cycle has no red fixers (a compile cycle, a batch's first run)."""
        tree = self.trees.get("fw")
        if not tree or not self.inherit("tracks") or not fixers:
            return None
        out = {}
        for fx in fixers:
            files = (touched.get(fx["task"]) or {}).get("fw") or set()
            out[fx["task"]] = sorted({p for f in files if "/vendor/" not in "/" + f and (p := gates.package_of(tree, f))})
        return out

    def fw_changed(self) -> list[str]:
        """Every framework package changed since plan.base: the set `test-run --fw` runs."""
        tree, base = self.trees.get("fw"), self.cfg.get("plan.base")
        if not tree or not base:
            return []
        return sorted({p for f in gates.changed_files(tree, base) if (p := gates.package_of(tree, f))})

    def fw_plan(self, fixers: list[dict], touched: dict) -> tuple[list[str] | None, dict | None]:
        """The framework crates of this cycle's trials: None for every changed crate, else the red fixers' own
        crates plus the crates whose trials failed in the previous cycle."""
        per = self.fw_crates(fixers, touched)
        if per is None:
            return None, None
        failed = ((self.prev or {}).get("tests") or {}).get("fw", {}).get("failed_crates") or []
        return sorted({c for cs in per.values() for c in cs} | set(failed)), per

    def test_part(self, part: str, args: list[str], log: str) -> dict:
        rc = self.tool("test-run", *args, log=log)
        if rc == 2:
            raise Stop(EXIT_TOOL, f"test-run {args[0]}: tool failure (exit 2); see {self.rd / log}")
        try:
            s = json.loads((self.runs / args[0] / "summary.json").read_text())
        except (OSError, ValueError):
            raise Stop(EXIT_TOOL, f"test-run {args[0]}: no summary.json")
        ps = s.get("parts", [])
        return {"exit": rc, "failing": sorted({n for p in ps for n in p.get("failing", [])}),
                "bad_binaries": sorted(f"{p['part']} {k}" for p in ps for k, b in (p.get("binaries") or {}).items()
                                       if b.get("status") in ("crashed", "not run")),
                "statuses": sorted({p.get("status") for p in ps}),
                "failed_crates": sorted(p["part"][3:] for p in ps if p["part"].startswith("fw:") and p.get("status") != "ok"),
                "passed": sum(p.get("passed", 0) for p in ps)}

    def tests(self, tracks: str | None, fixers: list[dict], touched: dict) -> dict:
        res = {}
        crates, per = self.fw_plan(fixers, touched)
        if "fw" in self.trees:
            if crates is None:
                res["fw"] = self.test_part("fw", [f"{self.a.label}-fw", "--fw"], "test-fw.log")
            elif crates:
                res["fw"] = self.test_part("fw", [f"{self.a.label}-fw", *(x for c in crates for x in ("--fw", c))],
                                           "test-fw.log")
            else:
                res["fw"] = {"exit": 0, "failing": [], "bad_binaries": [], "statuses": [], "failed_crates": [],
                             "passed": 0}
            if per is not None:
                res["fw"].update(crates=crates, per_task=per)
        if "app" in self.trees:
            res["app"] = self.test_part("app", [self.a.label, "--app"], "test-app.log")
        base = set(_lines(self.cfg.path("work.baseline_failures"))) if self.cfg.get("work.baseline_failures") else set()
        app = res.get("app", {"failing": []})
        app["new_vs_baseline"] = [n for n in app["failing"] if n not in base]
        before = set(((self.prev or {}).get("tests") or {}).get("app", {}).get("failing", []))
        app["fixed"] = sorted(before - set(app["failing"])) if self.prev else []
        app["new"] = sorted(set(app["failing"]) - before) if self.prev else []
        fw = res.get("fw")
        if crates is not None and fw is not None and not fw["failing"] and not fw["bad_binaries"] \
                and not app.get("new_vs_baseline") and not app.get("bad_binaries"):
            rest = [c for c in self.fw_changed() if c not in set(crates)]
            if rest:   # a green narrowed round: the other changed crates run before the cycle reports green
                r = self.test_part("fw", [f"{self.a.label}-fw-rest", *(x for c in rest for x in ("--fw", c))],
                                   "test-fw-rest.log")
                fw.update(rest=rest, rest_exit=r["exit"], failing=r["failing"], bad_binaries=r["bad_binaries"],
                          failed_crates=r["failed_crates"], passed=fw["passed"] + r["passed"],
                          statuses=sorted(set(fw["statuses"]) | set(r["statuses"])))
        if tracks and "app" in self.trees:
            branches = [x for m in getattr(self, "merged", []) if m.get("new") and m.get("pre")
                        for x in ("--branch", f"{m['task']}={self.trees[m['repo']]}:{m['pre']}..{m['sha']}")]
            self.tool("compare-runs.py", self.a.label, "--tracks", tracks, "--out", str(self.rd / "tracks.md"),
                      "--json", str(self.rd / "attribution.json"), *branches, log="compare.log")
            self.tool("diag-cut.py", self.a.label, "--tracks", tracks, log="diag-cut.log")
        return res

    def red_record(self) -> dict | None:
        """A red round's fixer models, pass delta (app tests passing now minus in the previous cycle) and the cost of
        the follow-ups it sent, for process/costs.md ("Red rounds by fixer model")."""
        sent = self.out.get("sent") or {}
        app = (self.out.get("tests") or {}).get("app")
        if not self.inherit("tracks") or not app:
            return None
        before = ((self.prev or {}).get("tests") or {}).get("app", {}).get("passed")
        return {"mode": self.mode, "models": sorted({v["model"] for v in sent.values() if v.get("model")}),
                "fixers": len(sent), "pass_delta": app["passed"] - before if before is not None else None,
                "cost_usd": round(sum(v.get("cost_usd") or 0 for v in sent.values()), 2)}

    def guard(self) -> list[str]:
        """The merge guard of a red round: a fixer whose merges compare-runs.py marks `likely` for more newly failing
        tests (that passed in the previous run) than its track fixed gets each of its merges reverted on the
        integration branches. Returns the reverted tasks."""
        try:
            att = json.loads((self.rd / "attribution.json").read_text()).get("tracks") or {}
        except (OSError, ValueError):
            return []
        out = []
        for task, a in att.items():
            bad, fixed = a.get("regressed") or [], a.get("fixed") or []
            mine = [m for m in getattr(self, "merged", []) if m["task"] == task and m.get("new") and m.get("sha")]
            if len(bad) <= len(fixed) or not mine:
                continue
            self.regressions[task] = bad
            for m in reversed(mine):   # newest first, so each revert applies to the tree it was merged into
                tree = self.trees[m["repo"]]
                r = git(tree, "revert", "-m", "1", "--no-commit", m["sha"], check=False)
                if r.returncode == 0 and m.get("restore"):   # the restored earlier commits go out with it
                    r = git(tree, "revert", "--no-commit", m["restore"], check=False)
                if r.returncode != 0:
                    git(tree, "revert", "--abort", check=False)
                    self.out["notes"].append(f"{task}: the revert of its merge {m['sha'][:10]} in {REPOS[m['repo']]} "
                                             f"conflicts; it stays merged; revert it by hand")
                    continue
                git(tree, "commit", "-q", "-m", f"cycle {self.a.label}: revert merge of {m['branch']} "
                                                f"({len(bad)} regressions, {len(fixed)} fixed)")
                self.reverted.setdefault(task, {})[m["repo"]] = {
                    "revert": git(tree, "rev-parse", "HEAD").stdout.strip(), "branch": m["branch"],
                    "tip": git(tree, "rev-parse", m["branch"]).stdout.strip(), "merge": m["sha"]}
            if task in self.reverted:
                out.append(task)
                track.event("revert", f"cycle {self.a.label}: merge reverted, {len(bad)} newly failing tests against "
                                      f"{len(fixed)} fixed", task=task)
        return out

    # ------------------------------------------------------------ 5. look
    def look(self, areas: list[str]) -> dict:
        if not self.cfg.get("look.driver"):
            return {"status": "skipped", "why": "look.driver unset"}
        args = self.cfg.get("look.port_build")
        if not args:
            return {"status": "skipped", "why": "look.port_build unset"}
        log = self.rd / "look-build.log"
        log.write_bytes(b"")
        rc = gates.run_logged(gates.cl(self.cfg, shlex.split(args)), self.trees["app"], log, self.env)
        if rc != 0:
            return {"status": "build-failed", "why": f"cl {args}: exit {rc}", "log": str(log)}
        panels = []
        d = self.cfg.path("look.states_dir")
        for f in sorted(d.glob("*.json")) if d.is_dir() else []:
            try:
                sts = json.loads(f.read_text()).get("states") or []
            except (OSError, ValueError):
                sts = []
            if not areas or any(str(st.get("map", "")).split(" ")[0] in areas for st in sts if isinstance(st, dict)):
                panels.append(f.stem)
        if not panels:
            return {"status": "skipped", "why": f"no states file in {d}" + (f" for {', '.join(areas)}" if areas else "")}
        rc = self.tool("look", "pair", *panels, log="look.log")
        return {"status": "ok" if rc == 0 else "failed", "exit": rc, "panels": panels}

    # ------------------------------------------------------------ 6. packets
    def packets(self, fixers: list[dict], touched: dict, compile_res: dict | None, lint_res: dict | None) -> dict:
        findings: list[tuple[str, str]] = []
        for repo, errs in ((compile_res or {}).get("errors") or {}).items():
            findings += [(repo, f"compile: {e}") for e in errs]
        for repo, fs in ((lint_res or {}).get("findings") or {}).items():
            findings += [(repo, f) for f in fs]
        groups = self.groups()
        owned: dict[str, list[str]] = {}
        unowned = []
        for repo, line in findings:
            path = line.split(": ", 1)[1].split(":", 1)[0]
            task = next((t for t, fs in groups.items() if path in fs), None) \
                or next((t for t, rs in touched.items() if path in rs.get(repo, set())), None)
            if task:
                owned.setdefault(task, []).append(f"{repo}: {line}")
            else:
                unowned.append(f"{repo}: {line}")
        diag_dir = self.rd / "packets"
        out_dir = self.rd / "followup"
        out_dir.mkdir(exist_ok=True)
        tasks = [f["task"] for f in fixers] + [t for t in owned if t not in {f["task"] for f in fixers}]
        branches = {f["task"]: f["branches"] for f in fixers}
        result = {}
        for task in tasks:
            pk = diag_dir / f"{task}.md"
            failing = _failing_in_packet(pk) if pk.is_file() else 0
            diag_left = any(git(self.trees[r], "grep", "-q", "DIAG ", br, "--", *sorted(touched[task][r]),
                                check=False).returncode == 0
                            for r, br in branches.get(task, {}).items()
                            if r in self.trees and touched.get(task, {}).get(r))
            mine = owned.get(task, [])
            bad = self.regressions.get(task, [])
            if not failing and not mine and not diag_left and not bad:
                result[task] = {"packet": None, "failing": 0, "findings": 0}
                track.status(task, "done", f"cycle {self.a.label}: nothing left on its list")
                self.give_slot(task)
                continue
            mode, trees = self.slot_for(task)
            L = [f"# Cycle {self.a.label}: your next round", "",
                 f"Fixer mode for this round: `{mode}`. Follow your prompt's section for this mode, on the same "
                 f"branches as before, and hand back the same way. Budget: about "
                 f"{self.cfg.get('pipeline.fixer_calls')} tool calls for this round.", "", *trees]
            if bad:
                L += [f"## Your merge was reverted ({len(bad)} tests that passed before fail with it)", "",
                      "The cycle reverted your merge on the integration branch: your change broke more passing tests "
                      "than it fixed. Fix these on your branch, keep your earlier fixes, and hand back; the next "
                      "cycle restores your reverted commits together with your new ones.", "",
                      *(f"- `{b['test']}`: {b.get('panic') or '(no panic line)'} ({b.get('why')})" for b in bad), ""]
            if mine:
                L += [f"## Compile errors and lint findings in files your commits changed ({len(mine)})", "", "```",
                      *mine, "```", ""]
            if pk.is_file():
                L += [pk.read_text()]
            elif diag_left:
                L += ["Every test of your list passes. Remove the `DIAG ` prints you left, in one commit."]
            f = out_dir / f"{task}.md"
            f.write_text("\n".join(L).rstrip() + "\n")
            result[task] = {"packet": str(f), "failing": failing, "findings": len(mine), "mode": mode,
                            "regressions": len(bad)}
        result["_unowned"] = unowned
        return result

    def slot_for(self, task: str) -> tuple[str, list[str]]:
        """The task's mode for this round and the packet lines naming its build trees. In build mode with a build pool,
        the task takes a slot (the one it holds, else a free one); with none free it works code-only this round."""
        if self.mode != "build":
            return self.mode, []
        pool = Pool(self.cfg)
        if not pool.exists():
            return self.mode, []
        try:
            k, slot = pool.take(task)
        except PoolError as e:
            self.out["notes"].append(f"{task}: {e}; it works code-only this round")
            return "code-only", [f"No build slot is free this round ({e}): work `code-only`.", ""]
        return self.mode, [f"Your build trees this round (build pool slot {k}; switch each to your branch first):", "",
                           *(f"- {r}: `{v['tree']}`, target dir `{v['target']}`" for r, v in slot.items()), ""]

    def give_slot(self, task: str) -> None:
        pool = Pool(self.cfg)
        if not pool.exists():
            return
        try:
            k = pool.give(task)
            if k is not None:
                self.out["notes"].append(f"{task}: build slot {k} given back")
        except (PoolError, SetupError) as e:
            self.out["notes"].append(f"{task}: build slot not given back: {e}")

    def groups(self) -> dict[str, set]:
        """{cfix-<stem>: the files the group owns}: its `<stem>.files` when present, else the files of its errors."""
        d = self.inherit("groups")
        if not d or not Path(d).is_dir():
            return {}
        return {f"cfix-{f.stem}": set(_lines(f.with_suffix(".files"))) if f.with_suffix(".files").is_file()
                else {l.split(":", 1)[0] for l in _lines(f)} for f in sorted(Path(d).glob("*.errors"))}

    # ------------------------------------------------------------ 7. send
    def send(self, packets: dict) -> tuple[dict, list[str]]:
        todo = [(t, p["packet"]) for t, p in packets.items() if not t.startswith("_") and p.get("packet")]
        if not todo:
            return {}, []
        st = self.board()
        if st and (st.get("paused") or {}).get("on"):
            self.out["notes"].append("the board is paused: no packet sent; send them with swarm.py --follow-up")
            return {t: {"ok": False, "error": "paused"} for t, _ in todo}, []
        timeout = int(self.cfg.get("pipeline.followup_timeout_min")) * 60

        def one(item):
            task, packet = item
            cmd = [sys.executable, "-I", str(TOOLS / "swarm.py"), "--follow-up", task, packet]
            # Own process group, so a stalled fixer's claude process stops with swarm.py.
            p = subprocess.Popen(cmd, stdout=subprocess.PIPE, stderr=subprocess.PIPE, text=True, start_new_session=True)
            try:
                out, err = p.communicate(timeout=timeout)
            except subprocess.TimeoutExpired:
                os.killpg(p.pid, 15)
                p.communicate()
                return task, {"ok": False, "error": f"stalled: no hand-back in {timeout // 60} min", "stalled": True}
            r = subprocess.CompletedProcess(cmd, p.returncode, out, err)
            try:
                j = json.loads(r.stdout.strip().splitlines()[-1])
            except (ValueError, IndexError):
                j = {"ok": False, "error": f"exit {r.returncode}: {(r.stderr or r.stdout).strip()[-300:]}"}
            return task, {"ok": bool(j.get("ok")), "error": j.get("error"), "cost_usd": j.get("cost_usd"),
                          "fresh": bool(j.get("fresh")), "model": j.get("model")}

        with ThreadPoolExecutor(max(1, int(self.cfg.get("pipeline.parallel")))) as ex:
            sent = dict(ex.map(one, todo))
        return sent, sorted(t for t, v in sent.items() if v.get("stalled"))

    # ------------------------------------------------------------ 8. board and records
    def phase(self, st: dict | None, batch: str | None, areas: list[str], compiled: bool) -> list[str]:
        if st is None:
            return []
        ph = st.get("phase") or {}
        cur, notes = ph.get("n"), []
        area = ",".join(areas) if areas else None
        if cur is not None and ((batch and batch != ph.get("batch")) or (area and area != ph.get("area"))):
            self.track_cmd("phase", str(cur), *(["--batch", batch] if batch else []), *(["--area", area] if area else []))
        if cur == 6 and compiled:
            r = self.track_cmd("phase", "7", "tests and red rounds")
            notes.append("phase 7 recorded" if r.returncode == 0 else
                         "phase 7 refused: " + "; ".join(l.strip("- ").strip() for l in r.stderr.splitlines()[1:-1]))
        return notes

    def upstream(self, green: bool) -> list[str]:
        """Notes for the lead: a sync that is due (portkit.sync.due), and on a green cycle, the early-CI command when
        land.early_ci_fork is set and the framework head is not the newest ref in <work.landing>/early-ci.tsv."""
        notes = upstream_sync.due(self.cfg)
        tree = self.trees.get("fw")
        if green and tree and self.cfg.get("land.early_ci_fork"):
            head = git(tree, "rev-parse", "HEAD", check=False).stdout.strip()
            f = self.cfg.path("work.landing") / "early-ci.tsv"
            rows = [l.split("\t") for l in f.read_text().splitlines() if l.strip()] if f.is_file() else []
            if head and (not rows or rows[-1][2] != head):
                label = re.sub(r"[^A-Za-z0-9._-]", "-", str(self.out.get("batch") or self.a.label))
                notes.append(f"early CI: tools/land/early-ci.sh fw {tree} {head[:12]} {label}")
        return notes

    def track_cmd(self, *args: str) -> subprocess.CompletedProcess:
        return subprocess.run([sys.executable, "-I", str(TOOLS / "track"), *args], capture_output=True, text=True)

    def weekly(self) -> float | None:
        cmd = self.cfg.get("pipeline.weekly_quota_command")
        if not cmd:
            return None
        r = subprocess.run(["bash", "-c", cmd], capture_output=True, text=True)
        m = re.search(r"\d+(?:\.\d+)?", r.stdout)
        return float(m.group()) if r.returncode == 0 and m else None


def _lines(f: Path) -> list[str]:
    try:
        return [l.strip() for l in Path(f).read_text(errors="replace").splitlines() if l.strip()]
    except OSError:
        return []


def _failing_in_packet(f: Path) -> int:
    m = re.search(r"^(\d+) of the \d+ tests on your list still fail", f.read_text(), re.M)
    return int(m.group(1)) if m else 0


def fw_step(c: Cycle, fixers: list[dict]) -> str:
    """The dry run's framework trials: every changed crate, or each red fixer's own crates and their union."""
    pending = [{"task": fx["task"], "repo": r, "files": git(c.trees[r], "diff", "--name-only", f"HEAD...{br}",
                                                        check=False).stdout.split()}
               for fx in fixers for r, br in fx["branches"].items() if r in c.trees]
    crates, per = c.fw_plan(fixers, c.touched(pending))
    if crates is None:
        return f"test-run {c.a.label}-fw --fw (every crate changed since plan.base)"
    own = "; ".join(f"{t}: {', '.join(cs) or 'no framework crate'}" for t, cs in per.items())
    return (f"test-run {c.a.label}-fw " + (" ".join(f"--fw {x}" for x in crates) or "(no framework crate)")
            + f" (red fixers' own crates: {own}); when that and the app run are green, the other changed crates")


def summary_line(c: Cycle, code: int) -> str:
    o = c.out
    parts = [f"cycle {o['label']}: exit {code}"]
    if "merged" in o:
        ok = [m for m in o["merged"] if "conflict" not in m]
        parts.append(f"merged {len(ok)}/{len(o['merged'])}")
    if "compile" in o:
        k = o["compile"]
        parts.append("compile: ok" if k["exit"] == 0 else f"compile: {k['fw_errors']} framework, {k['app_errors']} app errors")
        if k.get("unlinked"):
            parts.append(f"{len(k['unlinked'])} new file(s) no mod line reaches (unlinked.txt)")
    if "lint" in o:
        parts.append(f"lint: {o['lint']['count']} findings" + (", formatted" if o["lint"]["fmt"] else ""))
    if "tests" in o and "app" in o["tests"]:
        t = o["tests"]["app"]
        parts.append(f"app: {t['passed']} passed, {len(t['failing'])} failing ({len(t['new_vs_baseline'])} outside the "
                     f"baseline; -{len(t['fixed'])} fixed, +{len(t['new'])} new)")
    if o.get("guard"):
        parts.append(f"reverted: {', '.join(o['guard'])}")
    if "look" in o:
        lk = o["look"]
        parts.append(f"look: {lk['status']}" + (f" ({lk['why']})" if lk.get("why") else
                                                 f" ({len(lk.get('panels', []))} panels)"))
    if "sent" in o:
        ok = sum(1 for v in o["sent"].values() if v.get("ok"))
        parts.append(f"packets: {len(o['sent'])} sent ({ok} ok" + (f", stalled: {', '.join(o['stalled'])}" if o.get("stalled") else "") + ")")
    parts.append(f"mode {o['mode']}")
    parts.append(f"{o.get('total_s', 0):.0f} s")
    if o.get("stop"):
        parts.append(f"STOPPED: {o['stop']}")
    parts += [n.removesuffix(": run tools/sync") for n in o.get("upstream", []) if n.startswith("sync due")]
    return "; ".join(parts)


def report(c: Cycle, code: int) -> str:
    o = c.out
    L = [f"# Cycle {o['label']} report", "", summary_line(c, code), "",
         f"Started {o['start']}; phase {o.get('phase')}, batch {o.get('batch') or '-'}, area {o.get('area') or '-'}; "
         f"fixer mode {o['mode']}.", "", "## Times", "", "| step | seconds |", "|---|---|"]
    L += [f"| {k} | {v:.0f} |" for k, v in c.secs.items()] + [f"| total | {o.get('total_s', 0):.0f} |", ""]
    L += ["## Merges", ""]
    for m in o.get("merged", []):
        L.append(f"- {m['task']}: {m['repo']} `{m['branch']}` "
                 + (f"CONFLICT in {', '.join(m['conflict'])}" if "conflict" in m else
                    f"skipped: {m['skipped']}" if m.get("skipped") else
                    f"-> {m['sha'][:10]}" + ("" if m.get("new") else " (nothing new)")))
    if not o.get("merged"):
        L.append("- none")
    if "compile" in o:
        k = o["compile"]
        L += ["", "## Compile", "", f"compile-gate exit {k['exit']}: {k['fw_errors']} framework errors, app "
              f"{k['app_status']} with {k['app_errors']} errors. Logs: {c.runs / (o['label'] + '-compile')}."]
    if "lint" in o:
        lt = o["lint"]
        L += ["", "## Format and lint", ""]
        L += [f"- formatted {r}: {sha[:10]}" for r, sha in lt["fmt"].items()]
        for r, fs in lt["findings"].items():
            L += [f"- {r}: {len(fs)} findings in changed crates"] + [f"  - `{x}`" for x in fs[:40]]
        for r, fs in lt["outside"].items():
            if fs:
                L += [f"- {r}: {len(fs)} findings outside the changed crates (not counted)"]
    if "tests" in o:
        L += ["", "## Tests", ""]
        for part, t in o["tests"].items():
            L.append(f"- {part}: exit {t['exit']}, {t['passed']} passed, {len(t['failing'])} failing"
                     + (f", binaries crashed or not run: {', '.join(t['bad_binaries'])}" if t["bad_binaries"] else ""))
        app = o["tests"].get("app")
        if app:
            L += [f"- fixed since the last cycle: {', '.join(app['fixed']) or 'none'}",
                  f"- new since the last cycle: {', '.join(app['new']) or 'none'}"]
        if (c.rd / "tracks.md").is_file():
            L.append(f"- per track: {c.rd / 'tracks.md'}")
    if o.get("guard"):
        L += ["", "## Merge guard", ""]
        for t in o["guard"]:
            L.append(f"- {t}: merge reverted (" + ", ".join(f"{r} {v['revert'][:10]}" for r, v in o["reverted"][t].items())
                     + f"); newly failing: {', '.join(b['test'] for b in c.regressions.get(t, []))}")
    if o.get("red"):
        r = o["red"]
        L += ["", "## Red round record", "",
              f"Mode {r['mode']}; models {', '.join(r['models']) or '-'}; {r['fixers']} fixers sent; pass delta "
              f"{r['pass_delta'] if r['pass_delta'] is not None else '-'}; follow-up cost ${r['cost_usd']:.2f}. "
              "Add it to process/costs.md, \"Red rounds by fixer model\", when the port's numbers are collected."]
    if "look" in o:
        L += ["", "## Look", "", f"{o['look']['status']}" + (f": {o['look'].get('why')}" if o["look"].get("why") else "")
              + (f"; panels {', '.join(o['look'].get('panels', []))}" if o["look"].get("panels") else "")]
    if "packets" in o:
        L += ["", "## Packets", ""]
        for t, p in o["packets"].items():
            if t == "_unowned":
                continue
            s = (o.get("sent") or {}).get(t)
            L.append(f"- {t}: " + (f"{p['failing']} failing, {p['findings']} findings, {p['packet']}" if p["packet"] else "nothing left; done")
                     + (f"; sent: {'ok' if s['ok'] else s.get('error')}" if s else ""))
        un = o["packets"].get("_unowned") or []
        if un:
            L += ["", f"Errors and findings no fixer owns ({len(un)}): the lead groups them or fixes them.", "", "```", *un[:80], "```"]
    if o.get("stalled"):
        L += ["", f"Stalled fixers: {', '.join(o['stalled'])}. Read their logs before the next cycle."]
    fresh = sorted(t for t, v in (o.get("sent") or {}).items() if v.get("fresh"))
    if fresh:
        L += ["", f"Fresh sessions (context past pipeline.follow_up_max_context): {', '.join(fresh)}."]
    if o.get("notes"):
        L += ["", "## Notes", ""] + [f"- {n}" for n in o["notes"]]
    return "\n".join(L) + "\n"


def tsv_row(c: Cycle, code: int) -> None:
    f = c.runs / "cycles.tsv"
    o = c.out
    gap = ""
    if c.prev and c.prev.get("end"):
        gap = f"{max(0.0, c.t0 - T.parse_t(c.prev['end']).timestamp()):.0f}"
    o["gap_s"] = float(gap) if gap else None
    t = (o.get("tests") or {}).get("app") or {}
    vals = {"label": o["label"], "start": o["start"], "phase": o.get("phase") or "", "batch": o.get("batch") or "",
            "area": o.get("area") or "", "mode": o["mode"], "total_s": f"{o['total_s']:.0f}", "gap_s": gap,
            "errors": str((o.get("compile") or {}).get("fw_errors", 0) + (o.get("compile") or {}).get("app_errors", 0)
                          + (o.get("lint") or {}).get("count", 0)),
            "failing": str(len(t.get("new_vs_baseline", []))), "exit": str(code)}
    for step in ("merge", "compile", "lint", "test", "look", "send"):
        vals[f"{step}_s"] = f"{c.secs[step]:.0f}" if step in c.secs else ""
    new = not f.is_file()
    with open(f, "a") as out:
        if new:
            out.write("\t".join(TSV_COLS) + "\n")
        out.write("\t".join(vals[k] for k in TSV_COLS) + "\n")


def main() -> int:
    ap = argparse.ArgumentParser(description=__doc__, formatter_class=argparse.RawDescriptionHelpFormatter)
    ap.add_argument("label")
    ap.add_argument("--fixers")
    ap.add_argument("--tracks")
    ap.add_argument("--groups")
    ap.add_argument("--batch")
    ap.add_argument("--area", action="append", default=[])
    for step in ("merge", "lint", "tests", "look", "send"):
        ap.add_argument(f"--no-{step}", action="store_true")
    ap.add_argument("--dry-run", action="store_true")
    ap.add_argument("--config")
    a = ap.parse_args()
    if a.config:   # every tool the cycle runs reads the same port.toml
        a.config = str(Path(a.config).resolve())
        os.environ[config.ENV_CONFIG] = a.config
    try:
        cfg = config.load(a.config)
        c = Cycle(cfg, a)
        fixers = c.fixers()
    except (config.ConfigError, T.TrackError, Stop) as e:
        print(f"cycle: {getattr(e, 'why', e)}", file=sys.stderr)
        return EXIT_TOOL
    st = c.board()
    ph = (st or {}).get("phase") or {}
    areas = a.area or ([x for x in str(ph.get("area") or "").split(",") if x])
    tracks = c.inherit("tracks")
    c.out.update(phase=ph.get("n"), batch=a.batch or ph.get("batch"), area=",".join(areas) or None,
                 inputs={"fixers": c.inherit("fixers"), "tracks": tracks, "groups": c.inherit("groups")})
    if a.dry_run:
        print(f"cycle {a.label} (dry run): fixer mode {c.mode}; phase {ph.get('n')}, batch {c.out['batch']}, areas "
              f"{', '.join(areas) or '-'}")
        for fx in fixers:
            print(f"  fixer {fx['task']}: " + (", ".join(f"{r}:{b}" for r, b in fx["branches"].items()) or "no branch"))
        steps = [("merge", not a.no_merge, "git merge --no-ff of each fixer branch"),
                 ("compile", True, f"compile-gate {a.label}-compile"),
                 ("lint", not a.no_lint, "cl cargo fmt / clippy -D warnings / doc on " +
                  "; ".join(f"{r}: {', '.join(c.changed_crates(r)) or 'no changed crate'}" for r in c.trees)),
                 ("tests", not a.no_tests, fw_step(c, fixers) + f"; test-run {a.label} --app"
                  + (f"; compare-runs.py and diag-cut.py --tracks {tracks}" if tracks else "")),
                 ("look", not a.no_look, f"cl {cfg.get('look.port_build')}; look pair" if cfg.get("look.port_build")
                  else "skipped: look.port_build unset"),
                 ("send", not a.no_send, f"swarm.py --follow-up per packet, {cfg.get('pipeline.parallel')} at a time, "
                  f"timeout {cfg.get('pipeline.followup_timeout_min')} min")]
        for name, on, what in steps:
            print(f"  {name}: {what if on else 'off'}")
        for note in c.upstream(False):
            print(f"  {note}")
        return 0

    code = EXIT_GREEN
    compiled = False
    with track.recorded("cycle") as rec:
        try:
            merged = c.timed("merge", c.merge, fixers) if not a.no_merge else []
            c.out["merged"] = c.merged = merged
            touched = c.touched(merged)
            c.out["touched"] = {t: {r: sorted(fs) for r, fs in rs.items()} for t, rs in touched.items()}
            comp = c.timed("compile", c.compile)
            c.out["compile"] = {k: v for k, v in comp.items() if k != "errors"}
            compiled = comp["exit"] == 0
            lint = None
            if compiled and not a.no_lint:
                lint = c.timed("lint", c.lint)
                c.out["lint"] = lint
            if compiled and not a.no_tests:
                c.out["tests"] = c.timed("test", c.tests, tracks, fixers, touched)
                if tracks and "app" in c.out["tests"]:
                    c.out["guard"] = c.guard()
            if comp["app_status"] == "ok" and not a.no_look and "app" in c.trees:
                c.out["look"] = c.timed("look", c.look, areas)
            elif not a.no_look:
                c.out["look"] = {"status": "skipped", "why": "the app did not compile"}
            c.out["packets"] = c.packets(fixers, touched, comp, lint)
            if not a.no_send:
                c.out["sent"], c.out["stalled"] = c.timed("send", c.send, c.out["packets"])
            t = (c.out.get("tests") or {}).get("app") or {}
            fw = (c.out.get("tests") or {}).get("fw") or {}
            green = (compiled and not (lint or {}).get("count") and not t.get("new_vs_baseline")
                     and not t.get("bad_binaries") and not fw.get("failing") and not fw.get("bad_binaries")
                     and not c.out.get("stalled") and not a.no_tests and not c.out.get("guard"))
            code = EXIT_GREEN if green else EXIT_LEFT
        except Stop as e:
            code, c.out["stop"] = e.code, e.why
            print(f"cycle: {e.why}", file=sys.stderr)
        c.out["reverted"] = c.reverted
        c.out["red"] = c.red_record()
        c.out["notes"] += c.phase(st, a.batch, a.area, compiled)
        c.out["upstream"] = c.upstream(code == EXIT_GREEN)
        c.out["notes"] += c.out["upstream"]
        c.out["weekly_pct"] = c.weekly()
        c.out["lead"] = T.lead_sample()   # the cycle runs from the lead's shell: its session's cost so far
        c.out["end"] = utc(time.time())
        c.out["total_s"] = time.time() - c.t0
        c.out["seconds"] = {k: round(v, 1) for k, v in c.secs.items()}
        tsv_row(c, code)
        c.out["exit"] = code
        (c.rd / "report.md").write_text(report(c, code))
        (c.rd / "cycle.json").write_text(json.dumps(c.out, indent=1, ensure_ascii=False) + "\n")
        line = summary_line(c, code)
        t = (c.out.get("tests") or {}).get("app") or {}
        rec.result(line, log=str(c.rd / "report.md"), ok=code == EXIT_GREEN,
                   data={"label": a.label, "exit": code, "phase": c.out.get("phase"), "batch": c.out.get("batch"),
                         "area": c.out.get("area"), "mode": c.mode, "total_s": round(c.out["total_s"], 1),
                         "gap_s": c.out.get("gap_s"), "steps": c.out["seconds"],
                         "errors": (c.out.get("compile") or {}).get("fw_errors", 0)
                         + (c.out.get("compile") or {}).get("app_errors", 0),
                         "failing": len(t.get("new_vs_baseline", [])), "weekly_pct": c.out["weekly_pct"],
                         "reverted": c.out.get("guard") or [], "red": c.out.get("red")})
    print(line)
    return code


if __name__ == "__main__":
    sys.exit(main())
